From d6861c7c757cbc8df2b5a2c47c197cf18a10dd38 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 20:57:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02432/11362] [outer-loop] tr87 extended to L2: 1-to-many
 rewrite expansion + fresh_env

Operator: take a proper run at tr87 L2. RE'd the L2 delta from internal state.

L2 is NOT alter_rules (that flag is None at L2 -- it appears deeper). It
generalizes L1's substitution to a 1-to-MANY REWRITE: each target glyph expands
to a SEQUENCE of editable glyphs (B3->[C1,C5,C1], B5->[C2,C2]); the required
editable sequence is the concat of the rule RHS over the target sequence. The
verifier now computes required_editable that way -- subsuming L1 (RHS length 1).

Two fixes were needed to actually SOLVE L2 via the search (the direct greedy
solve worked, but the OfflineSolver best-first did not):
1. Verifier: bare mismatch-COUNT gives no gradient while cycling one glyph (drops
   only when exactly right) and EXPLODED at L2's 7 glyphs. Switched to SUMMED
   CYCLIC-DISTANCE -- each ACTION1/2 toward target drops it by 1 -- so best-first
   walks straight to the win. L2 in 152 states (vs blind BFS exhausting 52k+
   without even L1).
2. branch_mode replay -> fresh_env (gotcha #7): the win triggers a fade ANIMATION
   that leaves residual state (yfetxjexviz); a reuse-one-env replay search finds
   animation-contingent 'wins' that FAIL the reproduction gate (reproduced L1 by
   luck, NOT L2). A fresh env per candidate makes win-detection match the gate.

- solve_adaptered('tr87',2) -> reached_level=2, offline_reproduced=True (39 actions).
- 6 adapter unit tests (L1 1-to-1, L2 1-to-many expansion, cyclic-distance, the
  L3 length-gap bound, fresh_env branch_mode); all pass.
- metaharness 39-action replay -> L2; aggregate now 28 levels / 16 games (was 27/16).
- registry: L2 mechanic + the cyclic-distance + fresh_env gotchas + the L3 boundary
  (editable ALSO expands: tree/double_translation) recorded for the next attempt.

L3 RE (decode the editable-side expansion) is the documented next step; the L1/L2
verifier honestly leaves a >=7 residual there so the search stops, no false claim.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
